    "homeType": "MULTI_FAMILY",
    "description": "VACANT Victorian Duplex in prime Noe Valley, just one block from 24th Street's village corridor with cafes, restaurants and boutiques. Built circa 1900, this two-unit property showcases original period details while offering the perfect opportunity for a buyer's creative vision to bring it into the modern era. Great investment flexibility - owner-occupy, house hack, develop, TIC partnership for condo conversion, or traditional rental income. Featuring hardwood floors, wainscoting, high ceilings and plaster medallions throughout two light-filled, full-floor flats (2BR/1BA lower, 3BR/1BA upper). Dual-parlor layouts with pocket doors create flexible living space with bay windows and decorative fireplaces. Each unit has an enclosed back porch with laundry hookups. Upstairs, a classic Victorian fainting room' with balcony doubles as a bedroom, nursery or study. The large, deep lot features mature garden plantings with a lemon tree, flowering maple, oleander and more, plus a rear cottage and 2-car tandem garage offering potential for customization. Enjoy the sunny Noe Valley microclimate close to schools, Douglass Dog Park/Playground, Mission Dolores Park, and less than a mile to 24th/Mission BART. SF Victorian charm and investment potential in an unbeatable location."
  },
